{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 216 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>216</mn></mfrac></math> radians. The measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math> times the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine upper B\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math>?</p>", "keys": ["f372927b-31a0-4479-a897-22363f44566e"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "c8bc002c-cf17-4632-8eda-9f6458e39402", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "c067402e-060e-437b-886b-aa6d2a97f85e", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "ff26ce4f-b6fc-4b5f-b9db-872dbd0ce016", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction StartRoot 2 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "f372927b-31a0-4479-a897-22363f44566e", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction StartRoot 3 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<msqrt>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of angle <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math></em> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 216 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>216</mn></mfrac></math> radians and the measure of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> times the measure of angle <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math></em>. Therefore,&nbsp;the measure of angle <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi></math></em> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36 left parenthesis StartFraction pi Over 216 EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>36</mn><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>216</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math> radians, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math> radians. A trigonometric ratio can be found using the unit circle, or a circle with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> unit. For a unit circle centered at the origin in the <em>xy</em>-plane, the cosine of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math> radians is the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the point resulting from traveling a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction pi Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math> counterclockwise from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. This results in the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction StartRoot 3 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction comma one half right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper B\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction StartRoot 3 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"sine upper B\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cosine upper B\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>B</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "69d54aad-89b3-418d-8c94-c011d9fe97fd", "correct_answer": ["D"]}